  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Return and Reintegration Assistance for Migrants and Governments</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2023, IOM Tunisia has experienced a significant rise in requests for protection and assistance, including Assisted Voluntary Return and Reintegration (AVRR) for migrants in Tunisia. 1,910 migrants have voluntarily returned so far 2023 (as of 31 October) which exceeds the 1,614 voluntarily returns for 2022, demonstrating the increased demand for assistance.While prioritizing safeguarding the rights and well-being of migrants, particularly those in vulnerable situations, the project focuses on two key outcomes: providing case management services to the most vulnerable migrants, including those rescued at sea, and empowering migrants to pursue durable solutions, with a specific emphasis on AVRR. Through conducting vulnerability assessments, counselling, and assistance in return and reintegration, all aligned with IOM&apos;s guidelines, the project aims to bridge the gap between arrival and reintegration, addressing the immediate needs of migrants in Tunisia and facilitating their safe and dignified return to their countries of origin as one of the sustainable solutions.</narrative>
  </description>
